   [#D7D7AF]'Five-size phase presentation' section: extend [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]phase_size_presentation.py with an accessible five-step color ramp and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]canonical order so every chip, clan summary, and the distribution badge [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]render xsmall/xlarge beautifully; refresh visual snapshots.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Authoring guidance and explanation text[/bold #D7AFFF]                       [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]guidance[dim] · [dim][/dim]after core, aliases, routing[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]'Authoring guidance and explanation text' section: rewrite the epic [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`sase plan validate --explain` prose for all five sizes, remove the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]model-override testing exception in favor of xsmall, and keep it [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]consistent with the Rust schema descriptions.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]End-to-end verification[/bold #D7AFFF]                                       [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]verify[dim] · [dim][/dim]after core, aliases, routing, present, guidance[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]'End-to-end verification' section: rebuild the binding, run just check, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and exercise a scratch five-size epic plan to confirm validation, #plan [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]gating, per-size model routing, and rendered chips all behave.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-8w","llm_provider":"codex","model":"gpt-5.6-sol","phase_bead_id":"sase-8w.1","reasoning_effort":"xhigh","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-8ff9f9693d652554e65f97b084691567","started_at":"2026-07-23T21:39:17.556686+00:00","state":"active"},{"commits":[{"committed_at":1784845565,"sha":"39f90d3764eb050ae869f711a62e36f467874d64","subject":"feat(plan): document five phase sizes in --explain text (s